# New Window (⌘N) and New Incognito Window (⇧⌘N) from a window in full screen go full screen on a
# Space of their own, with ⌘N's command bar up once there, as in Safari and Chrome; from a
# windowed one they stay windowed (#528). It takes over Spaces, so it runs only with
# CRA_SCENARIO_SCREEN=1 (CI).
# promise: #528
requires screen
budget rss=700 stalls50=5
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=first
wait 3
cra://debug?fullscreen=1
wait 3
cra://action/newWindow
wait 4
cra://debug?windowState=new
expect-log window state new: main0 fullscreen=1
expect-log window state new: main1 fullscreen=1 visible=1 onSpace=1
cra://debug?commandBarRows=new
expect-log command bar rows new: open=1 mode=newTab
cra://dismiss
cra://action/newIncognitoWindow
wait 4
cra://debug?windowState=incognito
expect-log window state incognito: main2 fullscreen=1 visible=1 onSpace=1
cra://action/closeWindow
wait 3
cra://debug?fullscreen=0
wait 3
cra://action/newWindow
wait 3
cra://debug?windowState=windowed
expect-log window state windowed: main2 fullscreen=0 visible=1 onSpace=1
